  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is Kurla known for?",
      "answer": "Kurla is known for Phoenix Marketcity (one of Mumbai's largest malls), the Kurla railway junction connecting Central and Harbour lines, the LTT (Lokmanya Tilak Terminus) for long-distance trains, its proximity to BKC, and being one of Mumbai's most diverse and densely populated localities."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the pin code of Kurla?",
      "answer": "Kurla has multiple pin codes: 400070 (Kurla West / main Kurla), 400024 (Kurla / Nehru Nagar), and 400072 (Saki Naka / Kurla East border)."
    },
    {
      "question": "What are the sub-areas within Kurla?",
      "answer": "The main micro-localities within Kurla are Nehru Nagar, Kajupada, Halav Pool, Premier (Kurla West), Kurla East, Kamani, Tilak Nagar, and the Kalina belt."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the property price in Kurla?",
      "answer": "Property prices in Kurla range from ₹70 lakh for a 1BHK in Nehru Nagar/Kajupada to ₹1.4–2.0 Cr for a 2BHK near Phoenix Marketcity/Kamani, and ₹2.2–3.0 Cr for premium BKC-facing flats. Rental rates range from ₹16,000 to ₹55,000 per month depending on the sub-area and flat size (as of May 2026)."
    },
    {
      "question": "How to commute from Kurla?",
      "answer": "Kurla is served by Central and Harbour Railway lines at Kurla Junction (20 min to CSMT), Lokmanya Tilak Terminus (LTT) for long-distance trains, BEST bus routes from the Kurla depot, the upcoming Metro lines, and direct access to BKC, the Santacruz–Chembur Link Road (SCLR) and the Eastern Express Highway."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which hospitals are in Kurla?",
      "answer": "Major hospitals in and near Kurla include Bhabha Hospital (Kurla), Kohinoor Hospital, Holy Family Hospital (Bandra border), Criticare Hospital, and Sushrusha Hospital."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which schools are in Kurla?",
      "answer": "Notable schools in Kurla include Holy Cross High School (SSC/ICSE), Don Bosco High School (Kurla), St. Joseph's High School, Premier High School, and Oxford Public School."
    },
    {
